# Units that read the persisted store (/workspace/.substrate-private/, formerly the flat .substrate-secrets file) or /workspace/.substrate-secrets.d
# AT RUNTIME (not via EnvironmentFile=, which needs no exception) and therefore
# do NOT carry vessel.d/10-secrets-out-of-reach.conf. One list; nothing implicit.
# Format: <unit> <reason>. Read by validation/scripts/vessel-secrets-dropin.test.sh:
# every entry must be a real unit in units/ and must not carry the drop-in.
#
# No VESSEL unit is excepted. The entries below are the non-vessel units known to
# read or write the secret paths, declared so the boundary is explicit:
git-push-setup.service      setup-git-push sources the persisted store (/workspace/.substrate-private/substrate-secrets) for the push credential
identity-seeder.service     reseed-restart -> seed-identity writes METABOB_API_KEY / SUBSTRATE_ADMIN_KEY back into it
substrate-pull-sync.service runs vessel-ctl install, which sources secrets.env.sh, which merges into the file
#
# Not units, so not listed: gen-env runs from entrypoint.sh before systemd starts
# (it is the file's writer); operator tooling (substrate-key, substrate-config,
# config-surface-probe, spoke-federate) runs by docker exec, outside any unit
# namespace. A future secret-steward unit belongs in this list.
